# Line endings
#
# Biome (`pnpm lint`, `pnpm format`) enforces LF. Without this file, Windows
# clones with core.autocrlf=true get CRLF in the working tree, so `biome check`
# reports a format error on EVERY file — including ones nobody has touched —
# and `pnpm lint --write` rewrites ~265 files on each run.
#
# `text=auto` normalises to LF in the repository; `eol=lf` also checks out LF
# into the working tree, which is what Biome actually reads.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never touch these.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.eot   binary
